+In 為す, 為 writes な and す is okurigana, the kana ending that follows the kanji. な.る and な.す share the stem な; 為す uses な.す, so this card claims only what the linked word supports: 為す なす, JMdict 2861111, "word usually written using kana alone," and KANJIDIC2 lists な.す as a reading. 成す なす, "to form; to make; to constitute," is a separate JMdict entry whose fifth sense, "to do; to commit; to carry out; to bring about," is marked "word usually written using kana alone" with the note "also written as 為す." In 行為, [行](行.md), "go," supplies コウ and 為 supplies イ; in 作為, [作](作.md), "make, produce," supplies サク; in 人為, [人](人.md), "person," supplies ジン; in 為政者, [政](政.md), "politics," supplies セイ and [者](者.md), "person in a role," supplies シャ. 為 ため is also listed with the spellings 爲, marked "word containing out-dated kanji or kanji usage," and 為め, marked "irregular okurigana usage"; 為に ために is "for; for the sake of; to one's advantage; in favor of; in favour of; on behalf of." In 為替, the readings か, わ and せ do not belong to 為 or [替](替.md), "replace; substitute"; the whole word is read かわせ.
 
 The official Joyo table, the list of standard-use readings, shows イ with 為政者, 行為 and 作為, followed by 為替（かわせ）, a special reading listed for the whole word. The table lists no kun reading for 為; な.す and the other kun readings are outside the table. Practice selects な.す, the reading of the linked word article 為す. イ and the other readings are shown with dictionary examples or marked source-only and are not asked here; being outside the practice set does not make a reading invalid. The table shows the older form 爲 in round brackets, which this card does not teach.
 
